          deckDescription: 'One 32-card pack (Skat or Schafkopf style): eight cards per suit from Ace down to Seven. Four suits; total 120 card points (A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2). Used for Avinas trick-taking and point scoring; no jokers.',
          suitDescription: 'Four suits: in Avinas often played with French names (Clubs, Spades, Hearts, Diamonds) or German-suited pack (Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells). Eight cards per suit; follow suit when possible; trump order applies.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit: Ace (high), 10, King, Queen, Jack, 9, 8, 7 (low). In trumps the order is QC, 7 of trump, then other Queens, then Jacks, then A-10-K-9-8 of trump. In plain suits: A, 10, K, 9, 8, 7.',
